infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Who owns the value — and what each choice costs
  desc One input, two ownership models; when your code runs decides everything downstream
  compares
    - label Controlled
      children
        - label React state owns the value
          desc The value prop pins the DOM; onChange is the only door a keystroke comes through
        - label Re-renders per keystroke
          desc keystroke then setState then re-render, paid per character
        - label Buys live UI
          desc Validation, formatting, counters, dependent buttons — as the user types
        - label 5-15 ms per full-form render
          desc 40-80 ms with heavy children, so typing visibly stutters in wide forms
        - label Choose when UI reacts before submit
          desc Anything that needs the value mid-type
    - label Uncontrolled
      children
        - label The DOM owns the value
          desc Native browser behavior; React hears no individual keystrokes
        - label Renders once
          desc Your code runs only at submit time
        - label Read once via ref or FormData
          desc defaultValue seeds the initial text without claiming ownership
        - label Minimal re-render cost
          desc Nothing runs while the user types
        - label Choose for submit-shaped forms
          desc File inputs are always uncontrolled — code can never set their value
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
